# --- s045 Book I d.12 q.4 (priority of origin)
n("n734","s045-01","Quarta questio duodecime distinctionis","la","source","No fourth question on d. 12 in Scotus's *Ordinatio* as edited. The articles on order and priority of origin draw on *Ord.* I d. 12 q. 2, d. 9 and d. 20 (*utrum in divinis sit ordo*). The Scotist source of this compilation is to be identified.","to-verify")
n("n735","s045-02","sanctus doctor prima parte. q. 41. articulo. 3.","la","source","Aquinas, *ST* I q. 42 a. 3 (*utrum in divinis personis sit ordo naturae*): *ordo naturae… non quo alius sit prior alio*. A's *q. 41* is apparently an error for *q. 42*. In the Munich copy a contemporary hand has written ‘tho.’ in the margin here.","to-verify")
n("n736","s045-02","Augustinus. 10. de ciui. dei","la","source","The comparison of prior/posterior to order with even/odd to number has not been located in *De civ. Dei* X. The citation is as printed.","uncertain")
n("n737","s045-03","pridem prior primum","la","translation","Comparison: *prior* (comparative) and *primus* (superlative) presuppose a positive. Grammarians gave the adverb *pridem* (or the preposition *prae*) as the positive.","to-verify")
n("n738","s045-03","beatus Dionisius de angelica Gerarchia","la","source","Ps.-Dionysius, *De caelesti hierarchia* (cc. 6–10, the three triads ascending to the seraphim).","certain")
n("n739","s045-03","Augustinum de triplici habitaculo","la","source","Ps.-Augustine, *De triplici habitaculo* (PL 40, 991–998), on the vision in the heavenly homeland. Gorris's polemic (*salua gracia*) suggests that the attribution of the passage was disputed.","to-verify")
n("n740","s045-04","nulla res est que se ipsam gignat","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* I 1.1: *nulla omnino res est quae se ipsam gignat ut sit*.","certain")
n("n741","s045-04","Anselmum in Monologion primo","la","source","Anselm, *Monologion* c. 6 (nothing can be the cause of its own being, since it would be prior to itself). ‘primo’ is perhaps ‘in the first [book]’. To be checked.","to-verify")
n("n742","s045-06","prius a quo","la","source","*Prius in quo* vs *prius a quo*: Scotus's distinction of ‘signs’ of nature (*in quo*) and priority of origin (*a quo*). Cf. *Ord.* I d. 12 q. 2 and II d. 1 q. 1.","to-verify")
n("n743","s045-06","nulla illarum est a se","la","textual","As printed. The argument seems to need ‘none of them is from another (*ab alia*)’, since an order of origin requires one thing to be from another. B not checked.","uncertain")
n("n744","s045-06","But is there an order of nature in God?","en","translation","The Latin has no mark of interrogation. It is taken as an indirect question introducing the two school positions.")
n("n745","s045-03","Threefold Dwelling","en","translation","*De triplici habitaculo* (pseudo-Augustine).")

# --- B collation (full): B62R–B64L
upd("n735", append=" B also *q. xli.* (om. *sanctus*).")
upd("n736", append=" B: *aug. x. de tri. dei*, a conflation that does not help locate the passage.")
n("n984","s045-03","vsque ad vnum gerarcham","la","textual","B: *vsque ad vltimum ierarcham*.","certain")
n("n985","s045-06","nam sicut pater prius est quam filius. et prius spirat quam filius","la","textual","B: *Nam si pater prius est quam filius etc.*, om. *et prius spirat quam filius*.","certain")
upd("n743", append=" B agrees (*nulla illarum est a se*), so the difficulty is shared by both printings.")
n("n986","s045-06","in re absoluta","la","textual","B: *iure absoluto*, a corruption of A's reading.","certain")
